@if($assist->hasPackage('livewire/livewire', '^4.0'))
## Livewire 4

- Livewire 4 derives its update endpoint from APP_KEY (`/livewire-<hash>/update`). Never hard-code `/livewire/update`. When re-registering the route with `Livewire::setUpdateRoute()`, use the `$path` the callback receives; in tests, resolve the URI with `Livewire::getUpdateUri()` and find the route by its `livewire.update` name suffix.
- `addError()` adds to the error bag, which keeps earlier messages until the next validation or `resetErrorBag()`. A method that reports its own errors without `validate()` resets the bag first, or a field keeps showing the earlier message instead of the new one.
- Livewire 4 names an upload's MIME type from its **first 64 KiB** only (`TemporaryUploadedFile::detectMimeTypeFromContents()` runs finfo on that sample). A JSON or XML export whose sample ends inside embedded HTML is reported as `text/html`, and Filament's `acceptedFileTypes()` (a `mimetypes` rule) refuses it although the whole file is `application/json`. Validate such a file by its content — read it and parse it in a closure rule — and keep `acceptedFileTypes()` for formats identified by their header (images, PDF, Office files, video). No test can show the sniffing: under `runningUnitTests()` Livewire takes the type from the fake's metadata, so a feature test reports the misleading type on the fake (`UploadedFile::fake()->createWithContent(...)->mimeType('text/html')`) and expects the upload to be accepted.
@endif
